; The trigger for the privileged half of an agent update.
;
; THIS FILE IS THE INSTALLED UNIT, embedded into the agent binary and written
; verbatim to /etc/systemd/system/hcc-agent-update.path.
;
; # Why a path unit
;
; The unprivileged agent has to ask root to do one bounded thing. The usual
; answers are a setuid helper (a new attack surface, and one that is hard to
; get right), polkit rules (per-distribution configuration, and a surprising
; amount of it), or a D-Bus service (a daemon to write and harden). A path
; unit needs none of that: systemd already runs as pid 1, already watches
; paths, and the trigger is a file an administrator can read with `cat`.
;
; # PathExists, not PathChanged
;
; `PathChanged` fires on a write and would race a partially written file.
; `PathExists` fires on the file being *there*, and the agent creates it with
; a write-to-temporary-then-rename, so it appears atomically and complete.
;
; PathExists also re-triggers while the file remains, which is why
; `apply-update` removes the request before it acts rather than after: a
; crash mid-install must not become an install loop.

[Unit]
Description=Watch for a Homelab Control Center agent update request
Documentation=https://github.com/felixstaude/homelab-control-center

[Path]
PathExists=/var/lib/hcc-agent/update-request.json
Unit=hcc-agent-update.service

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
